---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";

const title = "Invoice vs Receipt: What's the Difference?";
const description = "Understand the critical differences between an invoice and a receipt, and when to send each document to your clients.";
const canonical = "https://invoice-generator.purohitansu7.workers.dev/blog/invoice-vs-receipt";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Navbar />
  
  <div class="pt-24 pb-12 bg-slate-50 text-center border-b border-slate-100">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-4">
        Invoice vs Receipt: What's the Difference?
      </h1>
      <div class="text-slate-500 font-medium mt-4">
        Last Updated: <time datetime="2026-09-16">September 16, 2026</time>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 prose prose-slate prose-lg">
      
      <p>For new freelancers and small business owners, the terms "invoice" and "receipt" are often used interchangeably. However, in the world of accounting and business management, they serve entirely different purposes in the payment lifecycle.</p>

      <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
      <p>An <strong>invoice</strong> is a request for payment sent <em>before</em> the client has paid. A <strong>receipt</strong> is proof of payment sent <em>after</em> the client has paid.</p>

      <h2>What is an Invoice?</h2>
      <p>An invoice is a commercial document issued by a seller to a buyer. It details the services provided or goods sold, the quantities, and the agreed-upon prices. Most importantly, it outlines the payment terms (when the money is due) and provides the client with instructions on how to pay.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Timing:</strong> Issued after the work is complete but before payment is received.</li>
        <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> To request money owed.</li>
        <li><strong>Key Elements:</strong> Due date, payment terms, and total amount due.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What is a Receipt?</h2>
      <p>A receipt is an acknowledgment that a specific payment has been received. It serves as proof of purchase and closes the transaction loop. Receipts are crucial for both parties for tax and accounting purposes.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Timing:</strong> Issued immediately after payment is received.</li>
        <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> To prove that a transaction has been successfully completed.</li>
        <li><strong>Key Elements:</strong> Amount paid, date of payment, and payment method used.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>When to Use Which?</h2>
      <p>If you just finished designing a website for a client and want to be paid, you send an <strong>invoice</strong>. Once the client wires the money to your bank account, you send them a <strong>receipt</strong> acknowledging the funds have cleared.</p>

      <div class="mt-12 p-8 bg-blue-50 rounded-2xl text-center border border-blue-100 not-prose">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Need to request a payment?</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 mb-6">Use our free tool to generate a professional invoice instantly.</p>
        <a href="/" class="inline-block bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold py-3 px-8 rounded-xl transition-colors shadow-sm">
          Generate an Invoice
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
